---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "About — aoblog";
const description = "What aoblog is, who's writing it, and why it's being built in the open.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold">About</h1>

  <div class="prose-plain mt-8">
    <p>
      aoblog is a build journal: a running record of designing a design
      system, a brand, and products with AI — plus a side channel of
      AI-assisted short fiction.
    </p>

    <p>
      I'm Andre Ortiz. I've spent twenty years in product design — vision,
      systems, and shipped work — and over the last few years a growing share
      of that work has involved AI agents as genuine collaborators, not just
      autocomplete. You can find my full background and portfolio at
      <a href="https://andreortiz.com">andreortiz.com</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      This site is organized around three threads — building a design system
      with AI, building a brand with AI, and building products with AI —
      plus <a href="/shorts">Shorts</a>, a collection of AI-assisted short
      fiction.
    </p>

    <p>
      It's built in the open: posts may be rough, plans may change mid-stream,
      and the <a href="https://github.com/andreortiz82/aoblog">source</a> and
      <a href="https://github.com/andreortiz82/aoblog/blob/main/PLAN.md">build
      plan</a> are public. That's the point — this is documentation of a
      process, not a polished case study after the fact.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
